  "reasoning": "To combine the fractions, we need a common denominator. The denominators are 5 and 4, so the least common denominator is 20. We rewrite each fraction with the denominator 20:\n\n$$
\\frac{4+6a}{5} = \\frac{(4+6a)\\cdot 4}{20} = \\frac{16 + 24a}{20}
$$
$$
\\frac{1+3a}{4} = \\frac{(1+3a)\\cdot 5}{20} = \\frac{5 + 15a}{20}
$$
\n\nSubtracting the second fraction from the first gives:\n\n$$
\\frac{16 + 24a}{20} - \\frac{5 + 15a}{20} = \\frac{(16 + 24a) - (5 + 15a)}{20} = \\frac{11 + 9a}{20}
$$",
  "tentative_answer": "\\frac{11 + 9a}{20}",
  "action": "handoff",
  "handoff_target": "A2",
  "handoff_note": "Verify the arithmetic and simplification steps, especially the sign of the terms in the numerator."
}

